  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) TCA 2-2-142(d)(1) (new)\n(quote) The online voter registration system shall compare identifying information submitted by the applicant, such as name, date of birth, Tennessee driver license number, or Tennessee identification number, with information maintained by the department of safety to confirm that the applicant has a matching record with the department of safety.\n(section) TCA 2-2-142(d)(4) (new)\n(quote) If the applicant's name and date of birth or other identifying information provided by the applicant cannot be verified by comparing the records of the department of safety, or if the applicant indicates that the applicant has not been issued a Tennessee driver license or Tennessee identification card, the online voter registration system may direct the applicant to complete, print, sign, and date the application and mail the application to the county election commission office in the applicant's county of residence to be processed.\n(section) TCA 2-2-142(c) (new)\n(quote) Any unique identifier, including driver license and social security numbers, shall be confidential and not subject to the open records law, compiled in title 10, chapter 7.\n(other) New 2-2-142(a): online voter registration available from July 1, 2017.\n(other) (b): the coordinator of elections builds a website to take applications, eligibility information under 2-2-104 and the 2-2-116 oath.\n(other) (c): a unique identifier per applicant; driver license and social security numbers kept confidential.\n(other) (d)(2)-(3): matching department-of-safety record lets the applicant finish online; the digital signature on file satisfies the 2-2-116 signature rule.\n(other) (d)(5): applications otherwise processed under 2-2-120.\n(other) (e): rulemaking and agreements with the department of safety.\n(other) Section 2: act takes effect July 1, 2016.\n(other) version: Draft 1294806 (2016-01-13): full text of the new online-registration section; identity match to department of safety records (slot e); no in-person ID, absentee ID or citizenship text.\n(other) version: Draft 1320038 (2016-02-02): same operative text; cover adds companion HB 1742 (By McCormick).\n(other) note: Enacted as Pub. Ch. 936, effective 07/01/2016 per the actions. The enrolled/chaptered text is NOT saved, and no amendments are saved or listed, so the enacted wording is assumed to equal the Draft but is not verified. The match is to a department of safety driver license or ID record; it is an identity match, not a citizenship check or proof of citizenship. In the House it was substituted for the companion HB.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
